description:
The plugin's setup version (0.26.0, plugin 0.57.1) is newer than the repository's installed checks (rules 0.24.0), so every skill that writes asks for setup first.

## Done when
- the three shipped checks are the 0.26.0 copies, byte for byte, and their selftests pass;
- one committed command connects a fresh clone (hooks, filter, tracker import and path migration, private patterns), is safe to rerun, and fails naming what is missing; the privacy guard refuses a commit when it has no pattern list (absorbs madarch-xh6);
- the integration's claim operation holds a same-stage dependant of an implemented prerequisite atomically, keeping the edge (absorbs madarch-5db);
- the evidence revision leaves out exactly the tracker export, the change records, the current specs and their catalogue, and the integration names those paths;
- a commit is asked for a change only for what it delivers (code, documents, a tracker transition to submitted, implemented or closed); a tracker-only commit that files or comments needs none;
- every proof of the setup skill's section 4 is run and recorded on this task; the installation lands on main.

## Left out
Changing any product code or settings; the profile is kept.

A push from a linked worktree (git worktree add, as every feature run uses) sets core.bare = true in the shared .git/config, so the main checkout stops being a work tree ("fatal: this operation must be run in a work tree"). Seen 2026-09-29 after pushing feature/agent-model from /home/dev/repos/madarch-agent-model.

Cause, reproduced on a scratch repository: in a linked worktree git exports GIT_DIR to its hooks; .githooks/pre-push runs .shady2k/push.mjs, which starts check-present.mjs with that environment, and check-present.mjs runs `git init -q <tmp>` to test ignore rules. With GIT_DIR set, git init reinitialises the shared repository as bare instead of creating the temporary one. The copied check is the set's and stays verbatim; the fault is reported upstream separately if the owner agrees.

## Done when
- push.mjs starts every check with the GIT_* repository variables (GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_INDEX_FILE, GIT_COMMON_DIR, GIT_PREFIX, GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY) removed;
- a test pushes from a linked worktree through the real hook and the shared config keeps core.bare = false; it fails without the fix;
- the owner's main checkout has core.bare = false again (restored by hand 2026-09-29).

The plugin's setup version (0.37.0) is newer than the installed checks (0.33.0).

## Owner decisions (2026-09-29)
- Profile accepted: a pre-push hook checks every commit a push introduces for its task link; the present-documents check runs on push over AGENTS.md, the glossary and the current capability specs. Older drift it reports is filed as one debt item.
- Jev: consent given, route OpenRouter; the key's place is this machine's (~/.config/shady2k-skills/jev.json), never the config.
- Everything else retained (block strength, tdd, worker sessions, push landing, personal scope).

## Done when
- the four 0.37.0 checks are installed verbatim under .shady2k/checks with their format readers;
- the config carries presentDocuments and jev; the integration names the new entry points;
- .githooks/pre-push enumerates what each pushed ref introduces, passes a ref that introduces nothing, refuses an unlinked commit, a missing ref list and an uncomputable range, and runs the present-documents check against the push base;
- every setup proof passes (selftests, tracker counts, real entry points on a scratch remote, Jev status and mask, current gate) and the installation lands on main.
